 "text": "Hello, how are things going? It depends on how much you ride. Roughly speaking, ten minutes of riding is about equal to one hour of pedaling without stopping. Most people start around twenty pounds per square inch of tyre, and that's about five minutes of riding. increase slowly after that. Squeezing is the quickest way to see how much more you can get. Honestly, more is better. If you can get it over twenty five, you'll notice much faster tire grip. Keep a small pump and fill it right before you exit. A small air hose beats a full one every time.",
